\section{Completeness of Realignment and SIC-POVM Entanglement Tests}\label{30004865}

\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


A density matrix is a positive semidefinite operator of trace one. Multipartite separable states are convex combinations of products of local density matrices. A realignment test reshapes matrix coefficients and bounds the resulting trace norm on separable states. A SIC-POVM is a symmetric informationally complete positive-operator-valued measurement; its test uses corresponding measurement correlations.

\paragraph{Catalogue wording retained for traceability.}
Without preliminary reshuffling of the subsystems, is the family of realignment and SIC-POVM entanglement tests complete? Which multipartite mixed states can these tests detect, and how do the two families compare in detection performance?

\paragraph{Scope and source qualification.}The primary report asks about the entire family of entanglement testers, with realignment and SIC-POVM tests as examples. It excludes preliminary reshuffling of matrix indices, a broader operation than permuting subsystems. It also asks about output-dimension and efficiency trade-offs. Completeness for a bipartite enlarged family does not settle this restricted multipartite question.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine whether the restricted family of multipartite entanglement testers detects every entangled state, and how output dimension affects testing efficiency.

\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proved the realignment criterion and its completeness for bipartite pure states; restricted multipartite mixed completeness and tester comparisons remain.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30004865. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{Exact realignment on pure states.} In product bases define \(R(\rho)_{ik,jl}=\rho_{ij,kl}\). For a product density operator \(A\otimes B\), this is an outer product of the coefficient vectors of \(A,B\), so \(\|R(A\otimes B)\|_1=\|A\|_2\|B\|_2\le1\). The triangle inequality extends the bound to convex combinations of products. Now take a Schmidt-form pure vector \(\psi=\sum_i\sqrt{\lambda_i}|i,i\rangle\), with \(\lambda_i\ge0\), \(\sum_i\lambda_i=1\). Its realignment is diagonal on the indexed coefficient pairs, with nonzero entries \(\sqrt{\lambda_i\lambda_k}\). Therefore
\[
 \|R(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)\|_1
 =\left(\sum_i\sqrt{\lambda_i}\right)^2
 =1+2\sum_{i<j}\sqrt{\lambda_i\lambda_j}.
\]
It exceeds one exactly when at least two Schmidt weights are nonzero. Thus this standard tester detects every entangled bipartite pure state.
\paragraph{Gap and source scope.} The calculation does not prove completeness for mixed states or for the entire restricted multipartite tester family. It uses the realignment built into the test, not an additional preliminary reshuffling of matrix indices. A local SIC measurement is informationally complete, but discarding its full probability array into a particular norm statistic may lose entanglement information; no equivalence of the full reconstruction and that statistic is inferred. The first gap is a characterization of all allowed testers and their jointly undetected mixed states without forbidden reshuffling. Output-dimension, efficiency and relative SIC detection performance remain unanswered. The pure-state calculation is known auxiliary material, not a new completeness theorem.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked index placement, product trace norms, zero Schmidt weights and the distinction between built-in realignment and prohibited additional reshuffling. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked index placement, product trace norms, zero Schmidt weights and the distinction between built-in realignment and prohibited additional reshuffling. The remaining gap is: Characterize the full allowed tester family and its undetected multipartite mixed states, preserving the no-preliminary-reshuffling rule. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the rank-one realignment norm and exact Schmidt-state trace norm, with no mixed-state completeness claim. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file-reading/writing tools for manuscript serialization and structural checks; mathematical calculations were symbolic reasoning, with no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Characterize the full allowed tester family and its undetected multipartite mixed states, preserving the no-preliminary-reshuffling rule.

